acpi: implement Match

The interpreter left DefMatch a todo!(): the firmware of a ThinkPad T15
uses it in a device's _STA or _INI, so the interpreter panicked before
the namespace was set up. Match interleaves its operands with two
bytes, the match opcodes, so it is in flight in stages, each reading
the next byte once the operand before it is done; the last compares
each element from the start index with both operands (the element on
the left, the operand taking its type: integers, strings, buffers) and
gives the first index for which both hold, or Ones.

Derived from acpi, so under acpi's license (MIT or Apache-2.0).

